  "body": "## What changed\n\n- The drill generator now writes the user's dwell into the `Cycle` record of a Back bore (G89) hole.\n- The Back bore chain now feeds out at the plunge feed. This is the same feed as the feed in.\n- The Sinumerik post writes `P0` for a G89 hole with zero dwell. This clears a previous positive dwell.\n- No golden file changed.\n\nFiles:\n\n- `crates/motion/src/drilling/cycle.rs`: the two changes above.\n- `crates/motion/src/drilling/tests_backbore.rs`: the two pinning tests (new file).\n- `crates/motion/src/drilling/mod.rs`: registers the test module.\n- `assets/posts/sinumerik.cps`: writes an explicit G89 P word, including zero.\n- `crates/post/tests/sinumerik_g89_dwell.rs`: pins the G89 dwell unit and the transition to zero.\n- `docs/decisions/1480-backbore-dwell.md`: the decision entry.\n\n## Cause\n\n`drill()` set the dwell of a Back bore hole to 0. The dwell of the user did not reach the cycle record, the simulation or a post.\n\n`drill()` also fed out at the cutting feed. A canned G89 has one F word, and the post takes it from the first cutting move of the hole, which is the plunge. The control fed out at the plunge feed, but the CL chain said the cutting feed. The verifier and the simulation read a different motion than the machine ran.\n\n## Dwell unit for each post\n\nThe posts read the dwell in seconds and write their own P unit. The Sinumerik post now writes G89 P at zero too. These tests pin the words:\n\n- Fanuc, Mazak, Doosan: `G89 ... P500` (whole milliseconds). `crates/post/tests/dwell_cycles_modal_p.rs`.\n- grblHAL, Tormach, LinuxCNC: `G89 ... P0.5` (seconds). The same file.\n- Haas: `G89 ... P500`. `crates/post/tests/haas_dwell_cycles.rs`.\n- Mach4: `G89 ... P0.25` (seconds). `crates/post/tests/mach4_post.rs`.\n- Sinumerik: `G89 ... P500`, then `G89 ... P0`. `crates/post/tests/sinumerik_g89_dwell.rs`.\n  Unit source: [Siemens ISO dialects Function Manual, 07/2021](https://cache.industry.siemens.com/dl/files/254/109801254/att_1077768/v1/ONE_840Dsl_828D_iso_dialects_fct_man_0721_en-US.pdf), table 6-1, printed page 95. Section 6.3.1 describes modal cycle parameters.\n- Heidenhain: an explicit chain with one `FUNCTION DWELL TIME` block. `crates/post/tests/heidenhain_cycles.rs`.\n- The lathe posts and the posts with no canned cycle refuse the Back bore by name.\n\n## Tests\n\nPins (`camcraft-motion`, lib):\n\n- `drilling::tests_backbore::back_bore_carries_the_dwell`\n- `drilling::tests_backbore::back_bore_feeds_in_and_out_at_the_plunge_feed`\n\nPost pins (`camcraft-post`):\n\n- `sinumerik_g89_dwell_posts_p_in_milliseconds`\n- `sinumerik_g89_zero_dwell_clears_previous_p`\n\nRed on unchanged code:\n\n- `back_bore_carries_the_dwell`: `G89 dwells at the bottom: the cycle record carries the user's 1.5 s, got 0`.\n- `back_bore_feeds_in_and_out_at_the_plunge_feed`: `left: Some(500.0) right: Some(100.0)`.\n\nMutations:\n\n- The old feed-out feed (`p.feed`) put back: `back_bore_feeds_in_and_out_at_the_plunge_feed` is red. Restored: green.\n- `CycleKind::BackBore` removed from the dwell list: `back_bore_carries_the_dwell` is red. Restored: green.\n\nGate on final head `766540356cab0fc156ea47466977f9432e0eeae4`:\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: PASS, 69 steps, 0 failed, 6.1 minutes. 1126 tests passed; 16 were ignored.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-motion -p camcraft-post --all-targets -- -D warnings`: PASS, no warnings.\n- `cargo xtask gate heavy --base upstream/main`: PASS, 217 steps, 0 failed, 27.5 minutes. The three checks for known failures in #1950 failed as expected. The gate accepted those expected failures.\n- Reached lanes: motion heavy and app heavy. Tested head: `766540356cab0fc156ea47466977f9432e0eeae4`.\n- Motion heavy: 56 tests passed. Two known-failure checks for #1950 failed as expected and the gate accepted them.\n- App heavy: 42 tests passed. One known-failure check for #1950 failed as expected and the gate accepted it.\n- Sinumerik mutations: removing the milliseconds scale made `sinumerik_g89_dwell_posts_p_in_milliseconds` fail (`P1`, expected `P500`). Restoring the scale made it pass. Restoring the old P condition made `sinumerik_g89_zero_dwell_clears_previous_p` fail (the second G89 had no `P0`). Restoring the fix made both tests pass.\n- Commands used `RUSTC_WRAPPER=` and `CAMCRAFT_NO_SCCACHE=1`.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone. `git diff --stat upstream/main...HEAD -- \"*.nc\" \"*.cl\"` is empty. No recorded program has a Back bore that the generator makes.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No test posts a generated Back bore with a dwell from the operation to the G-code in one run. The generator pin and the post pins meet at the `Cycle` record.\n- The Heidenhain post writes the Back bore as an explicit chain. Its retract line now has the plunge feed for a generated Back bore. The existing Heidenhain test uses a recorded chain and did not change.\n- The UI was not started.\n\n## Behaviour that changes for a program with no dwell\n\nA Back bore with no dwell keeps the same F. The Sinumerik G89 block now includes `P0` to clear a previous dwell. Its `.cl` chain changes: the feed out is now the plunge feed. The simulation time of the retract changes with it.\n\n## Overlaps\n\nNone. No open PR changes a file in `crates/motion/src/drilling/`.\n\nEffort: high\n\nChangelog: Back bore (G89) holes now carry the dwell at the bottom, and the toolpath feeds out at the plunge feed, as the canned cycle does. Sinumerik G89 clears the dwell when it changes to zero.\n\nFixes #1480\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
